  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe verb かく here means to go beyond or surpass (not \"to write\" or \"to scratch\"). The {裏|うら} refers to the hidden or unexpected side. The expression implies cleverness and is often used positively for strategic thinking, though it can also mean being deceptive.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {相手|あいて}の{裏|うら}をかく (to outwit the opponent)\n- {予想|よそう}の{裏|うら}をかく (to defy expectations)\n- {裏|うら}をかかれる (to be outwitted — passive form)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {出|で}し{抜|ぬ}く: to get the jump on, to steal a march — implies taking action before the other\n- {騙|だま}す: to deceive — more negatively connoted, implies dishonesty",
